{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_00-04-05-etcd_raft-real-run; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nupd={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Spending the remaining budget on a progress-axis suspicion I had flagged while reading tracker and never settled: whether a stale append rejection arriving while a follower's progress is in StateSnapshot can leave the leader probing from a regressed index, or stall replication. The source settles it, and the answer is no, so this is recorded as a refuted suspicion with its protective mechanism rather than left as an open hunch. It also documents that the progress axis was examined beyond the read-index question.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_maybedecrto\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"tracker/progress.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":226,\\\"end_line\\\":261,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_becomeprobe\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"tracker/progress.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":130,\\\"end_line\\\":152,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_isPaused\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"tracker/progress.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":262,\\\"end_line\\\":278,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_appresp_reject\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1505,\\\"end_line\\\":1520,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_msgsnapstatus\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1611,\\\"end_line\\\":1624,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@snapshot_progress_regression\\\",\n  \\\"parent_id\\\":\\\"ce33f7b508af4244883ac9c81a2a4696-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a stale MsgApp rejection that arrives while a follower's progress is in StateSnapshot leave the leader probing from a regressed index, or leave replication stalled, given that MaybeDecrTo is reachable in that state?\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_maybedecrto\\\",\\\"src_becomeprobe\\\",\\\"src_isPaused\\\",\\\"src_appresp_reject\\\",\\\"src_msgsnapstatus\\\"],\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"Suspicion: in StateSnapshot Next is PendingSnapshot+1, so a rejection from an append that was sent before the snapshot and carried index PendingSnapshot satisfies Next-1 == rejected, MaybeDecrTo takes its non-replicate branch and lowers Next below PendingSnapshot+1; the reject path only calls BecomeProbe for StateReplicate, and sendAppend is a no-op because IsPaused is always true in StateSnapshot, so the leader could probe from the wrong index or stall.\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Source: whether either snapshot outcome recomputes Next from PendingSnapshot rather than from the regressed value, and whether IsPaused keeps any probe from being sent from the regressed value meanwhile. A stall would require that no later event recomputes Next.\\\"}],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@snapshot_regression_self_healing\\\",\n  \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"The regression is transient and self-healing. MaybeDecrTo's non-replicate branch lowers Next to max(min(rejected, matchHint+1), Match+1) and clears MsgAppFlowPaused, but while the progress is in StateSnapshot (a) the reject path in stepLeader calls BecomeProbe only for StateReplicate, so the state is unchanged, and (b) sendAppend returns immediately because IsPaused is true for StateSnapshot, so nothing is sent from the regressed value. Both ways out of StateSnapshot recompute Next from PendingSnapshot: a MsgSnapStatus without a rejection calls BecomeProbe with Next = max(Match+1, PendingSnapshot+1), and one with a rejection first zeroes PendingSnapshot and then calls BecomeProbe with Next = Match+1. So a stale rejection in that state at most logs a decrement, and the snapshot outcome restores a consistent Next; no probe from the wrong index and no stall follows.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Captured snapshot, source reading only (no execution claimed): MaybeDecrTo at tracker/progress.go 226-261, BecomeProbe at 130-152, IsPaused at 262-278, the reject path at raft.go 1505-1520 and MsgSnapStatus handling at 1611-1624. The reachable trigger is a rejection for an append the leader sent before entering StateSnapshot, which under this source is the only way MaybeDecrTo sees rejected == Next-1 there.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_maybedecrto\\\",\\\"src_becomeprobe\\\",\\\"src_isPaused\\\",\\\"src_appresp_reject\\\",\\\"src_msgsnapstatus\\\"]}],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@snapshot_progress_regression\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_maybedecrto\\\",\\\"src_becomeprobe\\\",\\\"src_isPaused\\\",\\\"src_appresp_reject\\\",\\\"src_msgsnapstatus\\\"],\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"refuted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The suspicion is defeated by the surrounding state machine, and the mechanism is worth stating because it is what makes the counter regression harmless. The trigger is reachable - a rejection for an append sent before the snapshot satisfies Next-1 == rejected in StateSnapshot - and MaybeDecrTo does lower Next there, so the counter can be inconsistent with PendingSnapshot for a while. What prevents that from mattering is the pair of protections around it: the reject path upgrades to probing only from StateReplicate, so the state stays snapshot; IsPaused is unconditionally true in that state, so the sendAppend that follows is a no-op and no probe is issued from the regressed value; and both exits recompute Next from PendingSnapshot rather than from the regressed value (success keeps PendingSnapshot, failure zeroes it first, and either way BecomeProbe derives Next from Match and PendingSnapshot). The consequent replication therefore resumes from a correct index in both outcomes, which is the property the audit asks about. Nothing here is a defect, and no execution was needed: the state that would have to persist for a defect does not, and each step of that claim is a cited branch.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The counter regression itself is real and observable in the debug log line the reject path prints, so the account does not claim the value never moves; it claims the value cannot be used before it is recomputed.\\\"],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"Source reading only: no execution exercised the interleaving in this run, and the claim rests on the four cited branches rather than on a receipt.\\\",\\\"The trigger assumes an append sent before the snapshot can still be rejected afterwards; that ordering is allowed by the message model but was not produced here.\\\",\\\"A change to IsPaused or to either exit from StateSnapshot would invalidate this reading, so the two protections are cited explicitly for a reviewer to re-check.\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(upd,open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_00-04-05-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
